  "body": "PR #888 (`Fixes #887`) pins `ruststep` and `ruststep-derive` to an unreleased upstream commit through `[patch.crates-io]` in the root `Cargo.toml` - the workspace's only git dependency. The maintainer accepted it on 2026-11-11 \"for now, but drop it as soon as upstream is released\".\n\nBlocked on: a crates.io release of `ruststep` newer than 0.4.0 that contains the empty parameter list fix (upstream ricosjp/ruststep; its issue #256 asks for the release).\n\nWhen it is out: set `ruststep = \"=<new version>\"`, remove the `[patch.crates-io]` entries and their comment, let `Cargo.lock` return to the registry source with checksums, and run `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test import` plus the STEP suites.\n\nWhy it matters: a git dependency is only as available as the upstream repo, and audit tools read the lock's version (0.4.0) for code that is not 0.4.0.\n\nDone means: no `[patch.crates-io]` entry and no `git+` source for ruststep in `Cargo.lock`; the #887 fixture still imports.\n\nDepends on PR #888 merging first.\n",
